1
00:00:00,475 --> 00:00:01,325
A contour map

2
00:00:01,325 --> 00:00:01,912
is the ground

3
00:00:01,912 --> 00:00:02,962
in three D,

4
00:00:02,962 --> 00:00:04,075
drawn flat.

5
00:00:05,175 --> 00:00:06,212
Each line joins

6
00:00:06,212 --> 00:00:06,688
points at the

7
00:00:06,688 --> 00:00:07,738
same level.

8
00:00:07,738 --> 00:00:08,325
Here,

9
00:00:08,325 --> 00:00:09,650
every two metres.

10
00:00:10,770 --> 00:00:11,745
Lift every line

11
00:00:11,745 --> 00:00:12,295
to its own

12
00:00:12,295 --> 00:00:12,895
height,

13
00:00:12,895 --> 00:00:13,345
and the hill

14
00:00:13,345 --> 00:00:14,270
appears.

15
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:16,465
Lines close together

16
00:00:16,465 --> 00:00:17,940
mean steep ground.

17
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:18,952
Far apart means

18
00:00:18,952 --> 00:00:19,740
gentle.

19
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:21,485
Cut a section

20
00:00:21,485 --> 00:00:22,535
across them,

21
00:00:22,535 --> 00:00:23,085
and the ground

22
00:00:23,085 --> 00:00:24,410
profile falls straight

23
00:00:24,410 --> 00:00:25,010
out.

24
00:00:26,105 --> 00:00:26,780
Read the map,

25
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:28,030
see the ground.

26
00:00:28,030 --> 00:00:29,468
Free slope calculator,

27
00:00:29,468 --> 00:00:30,680
